{
  "id": "COMPOUND:37050 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "Annoreticuin-9-One is implicated in the regulation of Phosphodiesterase 6C through a complex network of targets. The evidence suggests that Annoreticuin-9-One acts as a target for LNCaP, which is itself a target of multiple compounds, including Rel-Plicatilisin B and CID 21582484. These compounds, in turn, direct their targets to Phosphodiesterase 6C. Additionally, Annoreticuin-9-One is linked to CX-1, which is targeted by Quercetin 3-O-Beta-D-Glucuronide 6''-Methyl Ester, another compound that also targets Phosphodiesterase 6C. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where Annoreticuin-9-One may influence Phosphodiesterase 6C through indirect interactions, possibly via the activation of downstream targets that ultimately modulate the enzyme's activity. The evidence supports a role for Annoreticuin-9-One in the regulation of Phosphodiesterase 6C, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
